name: Bounded systems context exposes coverage and never starts model or index work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_AGENT_MCPS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/systems_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: options systems-hunt:systems-context-gatherer
require-live-snap: 20 Max source bytes | context-options
keys: Down Down Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 Key: maxSourceBytes | aggregate-byte-option
ask: Are file, byte and surface bounds understandable before running this auxiliary context action, without suggesting Scan or complete Map progress?
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/context-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 partial inspection | bounded-context
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/systems_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | context-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: context-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: context-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: context-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: context-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: context-40x12-tail
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-01-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-02-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-03-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-04-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-05-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-06-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-07-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-08-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-09-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-10-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-11-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-12-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-13-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-14-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-15-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: context-reading-16-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/systems_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reader
ask: Are bounded source coverage, exact file paths, omissions and the absence of model/index work readable through keyboard paging at all six sizes?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape C-u
submit: run systems-hunt:systems-context-gatherer {"maxFiles":0}
require-live-snap: 20 must be at least 1 | invalid-limit
submit: run systems-hunt:systems-context-gatherer {"maxFindings":1}
require-live-snap: 20 unsupported by standalone systems context | unsupported-compatibility
ask: Do invalid and unused compatibility options fail clearly without producing findings, new jobs or hidden model work?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/systems_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART cli @TMP_HOME
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/context-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 partial inspection | restarted-context
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/systems_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | no-color-reader
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: no-color-40x12-tail
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-01-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-02-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-03-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-04-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-05-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-06-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-07-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-08-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-09-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-10-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-11-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: no-color-reading-12-40x12
ask: Does the restarted no-color reader retain usable navigation and honest partial-context wording without treating this action as a scan?
keys: q C-c
require-exit: 15
